IMPORT prelude

-- Public Utilities Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the water offences I can commit and what I can be made to pay: the penalty for each
-- offence (a statutory table, with s 58 for those that state none), the due-diligence defence and who loses it (ss 47(2), 47A(3),
-- 50(6), 56A), the storage-tank duties (s 45A), whom I may engage for plumbing and water-service design work (ss 40G, 40H and the
-- s 2 definitions), the duty to enquire before I dig (s 57), my notice as a 5% controller (ss 44A, 44E, 44J) and composition (s 59).
--
-- SEAT: the consumer -- the owner or occupier of premises supplied with water, and anyone who digs near, connects to, draws from or
-- works on the water system -- to whom the Act's prohibitions and penalties are applied.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("limited WSI design works", "regulated works", "WSI design works"); ss 26(6), 33(2)(a), 34(2), 37(1),
-- 39, 40G(1) to (9), 40H, 41(1), (2), 44A(1) ("5% controller"), 44E, 44J, 45(7), 45A(1) to (5), 46, 47(1), (2), (6), 47A(1) to (3),
-- (7), 48(1), 49, 50(1), (2), (6), 51, 52, 55(3), 56A, 57(1), 58, 59(1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 29 May 2026 (amendments to Act 8 of 2026 shown), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PUA2001.txt. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit (agent liability is s 56A,
-- the excavation duty s 57), which the cross-references in ss 47(2) and 47A(3) confirm.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Board's constitution, finances and funds (Part 2, Schedules); plumber licensing procedure and the duties of
-- licensed plumbers and engineers (ss 40I to 40Q); approved suppliers' conditions and financial penalties (ss 41(3) to 44); the
-- 12%, 30% and indirect controller approvals, remedial directions and special administration (ss 44F to 44M); the evidential
-- presumptions in s 50(3) to (5); investigation powers (ss 55A, 55B) beyond the offence in s 55(3); body-corporate officers (s 56);
-- Parts 6 and 7. No regulations were deposited, so the persons "responsible" for maintenance and tank security (ss 45(8), 45A(7)),
-- the works excluded from "regulated works" by order, and the offences "prescribed as compoundable" (s 59(1)(b)) are asked as facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE AS ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Utilities Act 2001 -- what I can be made to pay`

§§ `Penalties -- each offence, and s 58 for the rest`

-- s 58: "Any person guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is expressly provided shall be liable on conviction to
-- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- offence, to a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction."
-- Express penalties read in the body: s 26(6) "a fine not exceeding $20,000"; s 33(2)(a) $10,000 or 12 months; s 34(2) "a fine not
-- exceeding $5,000"; s 37(1) $10,000 and $250 a day; s 40G(7) $10,000 or 3 years; s 41(2) $50,000 or 5 YEARS; s 45A(5) $50,000 or
-- 12 months and $1,000 a day; s 47(1) $10,000 or 3 years; s 47A(1)(a) $40,000 or 3 MONTHS, (b) "if the water main or connecting
-- pipe is 300 mm or more in diameter" $200,000 or 3 years; s 47A(2) $200,000 or 3 years; s 50(1) $50,000 or 3 years and $1,000 a
-- day; s 50(2) $50,000 or 3 years and $2,500 a day; s 55(3) "a fine not exceeding $5,000"; s 57(1) $50,000 or 3 years.
-- Sections 39(4), 40G(8), 40H(2), 45(7), 46(3), 47(6), 47A(7), 49, 51 and 52 create offences with no penalty of their own.
-- A zero term means the provision allows no imprisonment; a zero daily fine means it gives none for a continuing offence.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 26 relocating or altering a Board water installation without approval`
    `s 33 failing to remove an obstruction to a Board installation`
    `s 34 not reporting a pipe wasting water`
    `s 37 using a supply reinstated without authority`
    `s 39 entering Board premises without written consent`
    `s 40G(1)-(4) carrying out regulated works unlicensed`
    `s 40G(5)-(6) or 40H engaging the wrong person`
    `s 41 supplying drinking water without approval`
    `s 45 failing to maintain my water service installation`
    `s 45A(1)-(2) failing to secure a drinking-water storage tank`
    `s 45A(4) entering or opening a storage tank without permission`
    `s 46 failing to mark or separate pipes`
    `s 47 damaging Board property`
    `s 47 or 47A failing to comply with a restoration notice`
    `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm`
    `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more`
    `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply`
    `s 49 pretending to be a Board employee to get in`
    `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption`
    `s 50(2)(a) dishonestly abstracting water`
    `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent`
    `s 50(2)(c) interfering with a meter`
    `s 50(2)(d) altering or tampering with a meter`
    `s 51 obstructing the Board`
    `s 52 making a false statement`
    `s 55 refusing to give my identity`
    `s 57 digging without enquiring first`

DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `the most I can be fined`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the longest term in months`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the most I can be fined for each further day` IS A NUMBER

`the general penalty under s 58` MEANS Penalty OF 10000, 12, 250

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A Penalty
`the penalty for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    --                                                                                  fine,    months, daily
    WHEN `s 26 relocating or altering a Board water installation without approval` THEN Penalty OF  20000,  0,      0
    WHEN `s 33 failing to remove an obstruction to a Board installation`           THEN Penalty OF  10000,  12,     0
    WHEN `s 34 not reporting a pipe wasting water`                                 THEN Penalty OF  5000,   0,      0
    WHEN `s 37 using a supply reinstated without authority`                        THEN Penalty OF  10000,  0,      250
    WHEN `s 40G(1)-(4) carrying out regulated works unlicensed`                    THEN Penalty OF  10000,  36,     0
    WHEN `s 41 supplying drinking water without approval`                          THEN Penalty OF  50000,  60,     0
    WHEN `s 45A(1)-(2) failing to secure a drinking-water storage tank`            THEN Penalty OF  50000,  12,     1000
    WHEN `s 45A(4) entering or opening a storage tank without permission`          THEN Penalty OF  50000,  12,     1000
    WHEN `s 47 damaging Board property`                                            THEN Penalty OF  10000,  36,     0
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm`                             THEN Penalty OF  40000,  3,      0
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more`                        THEN Penalty OF  200000, 36,     0
    WHEN `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply`      THEN Penalty OF  200000, 36,     0
    WHEN `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption`     THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     1000
    WHEN `s 50(2)(a) dishonestly abstracting water`                                THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     2500
    WHEN `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent`                        THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     2500
    WHEN `s 50(2)(c) interfering with a meter`                                     THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     2500
    WHEN `s 50(2)(d) altering or tampering with a meter`                           THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     2500
    WHEN `s 55 refusing to give my identity`                                       THEN Penalty OF  5000,   0,      0
    WHEN `s 57 digging without enquiring first`                                    THEN Penalty OF  50000,  36,     0
    OTHERWISE `the general penalty under s 58`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS (`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `the most I can be fined`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` MEANS (`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `the longest term in months`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for each day the offence continues after conviction` MEANS
    (`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `the most I can be fined for each further day`

-- s 47A(1): the tier turns on the diameter alone -- "300 mm or more in diameter" -- whether I damaged it "wilfully or otherwise".
-- s 48(1): compensation for the damage is payable "in addition to any penalty", and is not computed here.
GIVEN `the diameter of the main in mm` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Offence
`Which s 47A(1) offence is damaging this main` MEANS
    IF   `the diameter of the main in mm` AT LEAST 300
    THEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more`
    ELSE `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm`

§§ `ss 47(2), 47A(3), 50(6), 56A -- the due-diligence defence, and my liability for my employee`

-- s 47(2), s 47A(3): "it is a defence ... to prove that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence
-- to avoid the commission of the offence, but this defence is not available to any person who may be liable by virtue of section
-- 56A". s 50(6): the same defence "In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (1) or (2)(b) or (d)", for the person charged
-- "(but not by virtue of section 56A)". So dishonest abstraction (s 50(2)(a)) and meter interference (s 50(2)(c)) have no such
-- defence, and neither has any other offence in scope.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the offence carry a due-diligence defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 47 damaging Board property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(2)(d) altering or tampering with a meter` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
      `I am charged only as the employer or principal under s 56A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove I took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I escape conviction on the due-diligence defence` IF
        `Does the offence carry a due-diligence defence` `the offence`
    AND NOT `I am charged only as the employer or principal under s 56A`
    AND `I prove I took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence`

-- s 56A: where an offence is committed by my agent or employee, or a person under my supervision or instruction in the course of the
-- employment, I "shall ... be liable for that offence in the same manner and to the same extent as if [I] had personally committed
-- the offence unless [I prove] to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was committed without the consent or connivance,
-- and that it was not attributable to any neglect on the part, of that other person". Both limbs must be proved.
GIVEN `my agent or employee committed the offence in the course of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove it was without my consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove it was not attributable to any neglect of mine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable for my employee's offence` IF
        `my agent or employee committed the offence in the course of the employment`
    AND NOT (`I prove it was without my consent or connivance` AND `I prove it was not attributable to any neglect of mine`)

§§ `s 45A -- my storage tank`

-- s 45A(1): "A person responsible for the security of a water service installation having a storage tank from which piped water
-- suitable for drinking (excluding NEWater) is drawn must ensure that" the tank, its taps and appurtenances and the premises where
-- they are "are secured against unauthorised access and tampering". (2) adds: access only with my authority, kept "properly locked
-- at all times", regular checks, proper records open to inspection, and notifying the Board "without delay" of unauthorised access.
-- (3): "Subsection (2) does not apply to a person responsible for the security of a water service installation having any storage
-- tank in residential premises which do not take their water supply through a master meter." The duty in (1) still applies.
-- s 2: "storage tank" means a tank or cistern with a free water surface under atmospheric pressure, but not "(a) a flushing cistern;
-- or (b) a drinking-trough or drinking-bowl for animals". Who is "responsible" is left to regulations (s 45A(7)), not deposited, so
-- it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My tank` HAS
    `I am the person responsible for the security of the installation`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 45A(7), regulations not deposited
    `it has a free water surface under atmospheric pressure`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a flushing cistern or an animal drinking-trough or bowl`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `drinking water is drawn from it`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it holds only NEWater`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are residential`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises take their supply through a master meter`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2: a meter with sub-meters

DECLARE `Tank duties` IS ONE OF
    `no s 45A duty falls on me`
    `only the general duty to secure the tank against unauthorised access and tampering`
    `the general duty and the detailed duties: authorised access, locked, checked, recorded, reported`

GIVEN `the tank` IS A `My tank`
GIVETH A `Tank duties`
DECIDE `Which storage tank security duties must I meet` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 45A reaches the tank and me`
            THEN `no s 45A duty falls on me`
        IF `the tank`'s `the premises are residential` AND NOT `the tank`'s `the premises take their supply through a master meter`
            THEN `only the general duty to secure the tank against unauthorised access and tampering`
        OTHERWISE `the general duty and the detailed duties: authorised access, locked, checked, recorded, reported`
  WHERE
    `s 45A reaches the tank and me` MEANS
            `the tank`'s `I am the person responsible for the security of the installation`
        AND `the tank`'s `it has a free water surface under atmospheric pressure`
        AND NOT `the tank`'s `it is a flushing cistern or an animal drinking-trough or bowl`
        AND `the tank`'s `drinking water is drawn from it`
        AND NOT `the tank`'s `it holds only NEWater`

§§ `ss 2, 40G, 40H -- whom I may engage for plumbing and design work`

-- s 2: "limited WSI design works" means "the designing of any water service installation that is to be installed downstream of a
-- meter, where the water service installation being designed does not include any pumping equipment or storage tank". "WSI design
-- works" is the designing of any water service installation. "regulated works" means "any sanitary works, limited WSI design works
-- or WSI works", less works excluded by Ministerial order (none deposited).
GIVEN `the design includes pumping equipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the design includes a storage tank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my design work limited WSI design works` IF
    NOT `the design includes pumping equipment` AND NOT `the design includes a storage tank`

DECLARE Work IS ONE OF
    `sanitary works`                -- s 2: drain-lines, discharge pipes, sanitary appliances
    `WSI works`                     -- work on a water service installation
    `limited WSI design works`      -- design with no pump or storage tank
    `other WSI design works`        -- design with a pump or storage tank

DECLARE Engagee IS ONE OF
    `a licensed plumber`
    `a business whose works are done by or under licensed plumbers`
    `a professional engineer who is not a licensed plumber`
    `an unlicensed handyman`

-- s 40G(5): an owner or occupier wanting sanitary works or WSI works "must only engage a person permitted under subsection (1) or
-- (3)" -- an individual who is a licensed plumber or acts under one's direct supervision, or a business that ensures the works are
-- so carried out. (6): for limited WSI design works, such a person "or (b) a professional engineer". s 40H(1): for WSI design works
-- that "are not limited WSI design works", "only engage a professional engineer". s 40G(9): (1) to (4) do not apply "to a
-- professional engineer in respect of any limited WSI design works". Breach by me is an offence under ss 40G(8), 40H(2).
GIVEN `the person` IS AN Engagee, `the work` IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I engage this person for the work` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`
    WHEN `other WSI design works` THEN `the person` EQUALS `a professional engineer who is not a licensed plumber`
    WHEN `limited WSI design works` THEN NOT (`the person` EQUALS `an unlicensed handyman`)
    OTHERWISE `the person` EQUALS `a licensed plumber` OR `the person` EQUALS `a business whose works are done by or under licensed plumbers`

§§ `s 57 -- before I dig`

-- s 57(1): any person who "digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates, tunnels or breaks any ground with any mechanical equipment, tool
-- or explosive, or allows the person's employee or agent to do so, without first -- (a) obtaining from the Board the relevant plans
-- or records ...; (b) carrying out trial trenches to physically ascertain the location of any such main or pipe ...; and (c)
-- complying with any other requirements that the Board may specify" is guilty of an offence. All three are required.
GIVEN `I or my employee break ground with equipment, a tool or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I first obtained the Board's plans or records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I first dug trial trenches` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I first complied with the Board's other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would my digging be an offence` IF
        `I or my employee break ground with equipment, a tool or explosive`
    AND NOT (    `I first obtained the Board's plans or records`
             AND `I first dug trial trenches`
             AND `I first complied with the Board's other requirements`)

§§ `ss 44A, 44E, 44J -- if I hold 5% of a designated water entity`

-- s 44A(1): a "5% controller" is a person who, alone or with associates, "holds 5% or more, but less than 12%, of the total equity
-- interests in" or controls that share of the voting power in a designated entity, business trust or trust. s 44E(1): a person who
-- becomes one "on or after 1 April 2020" must "within 7 days after becoming the 5% controller, give written notice to the Board".
-- Defences: (3) "was not aware of the contravention when it occurred" and notified "within a period of 14 days after becoming aware";
-- (4) the crossing came from an associate's increase, with "no agreement or arrangement" with that associate, and notice "within a
-- period of 7 days after the contravention". (5): otherwise lack of intent is no defence.
GIVEN `the percentage I hold or control with my associates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a 5% controller` IF
    `the percentage I hold or control with my associates` AT LEAST 5 AND `the percentage I hold or control with my associates` LESS THAN 12

DECLARE `My notice` HAS
    `the date I became a 5% controller`                              IS A DATE
    `days after becoming one that I notified the Board`              IS A NUMBER
    `I was unaware of the contravention when it occurred`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after becoming aware that I notified the Board`            IS A NUMBER
    `it came from an associate's increase with no arrangement between us` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the contravention that I notified the Board`         IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence by notifying the Board late` IF
        DATE_SERIAL (`the notice`'s `the date I became a 5% controller`) AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2020)
    AND `the notice`'s `days after becoming one that I notified the Board` GREATER THAN 7
    AND NOT (    `the notice`'s `I was unaware of the contravention when it occurred`
             AND `the notice`'s `days after becoming aware that I notified the Board` AT MOST 14)
    AND NOT (    `the notice`'s `it came from an associate's increase with no arrangement between us`
             AND `the notice`'s `days after the contravention that I notified the Board` AT MOST 7)

-- s 44J: "(a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not exceeding $500,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or
-- to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $50,000 for every day ...; or (b) in any other
-- case, to a fine not exceeding $1 million" and $100,000 a day.
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Penalty
`What can I be made to pay for a Part 4A Division 2 offence` MEANS
    IF `I am an individual` THEN Penalty OF 500000, 36, 50000 ELSE Penalty OF 1000000, 0, 100000

§§ `s 59 -- may I compound the offence`

-- s 59(1): the Board may "(a) compound any offence under section 45A by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having
-- committed the offence a sum not exceeding $10,000; and (b) compound any other offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence ... a sum not exceeding $3,000". Which offences are prescribed is in regulations not deposited, so it is asked
-- as a fact. Composition is the Board's to offer; NOTHING means the Act offers no composition for that offence.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 45A(1)-(2) failing to secure a drinking-water storage tank` THEN JUST 10000
    WHEN `s 45A(4) entering or opening a storage tank without permission` THEN JUST 10000
    OTHERWISE IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` THEN JUST 3000 ELSE NOTHING
